---
KB CLI MVP command surface

Usage: kb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init         
  add          
  mv           
  rm           
  path         
  chmod        
  list         
  check        
  update       
  ask          
  remember     
  correct      
  consolidate  
  env          
  serve        
  completion   

Options:
      --output <OUTPUT>
          Possible values:
          - text: 面向用户的可读输出。
          - json: 面向机器消费的结构化 JSON 输出。
          
          [default: text]

      --quiet
          

  -v, --verbose...
          

      --no-color
          

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

These are common kb commands used in various situations:

start a working area
  init        Create kb.md, .kb state and default ignore rules

manage references
  add         Add file contents to the knowledge base
  mv          Move or rename an alias
  rm          Remove an alias from the working set
  path        Show or update the path of an alias
  chmod       Update permissions of an alias
  list        List tracked aliases

maintain index state
  check       Show index diff without writing files
  update      Apply index diff and persist snapshot (use --strict for L2-L5 hard-fail)

build agent memory
  remember    Record an agent observation into the L0 episode timeline
  correct     Record a user correction (highest-priority memory signal)
  consolidate Distill accumulated episodes into agent-memory files

retrieve and environment
  ask         Retrieve relevant context for a question
  serve       Serve the memory system over stdio JSON-RPC (MCP) for external agents
  env         Show registered knowledge base roots
  completion  Generate shell completion scripts
